---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Sampling diagram"
  title="Predict noise, form the mean, then take one reverse step"
  caption="An editorial reconstruction connecting page 44's noise-prediction mean to the original DDPM sampling algorithm. Start with xT drawn from N(0,I) and repeat from T down to 1. This diagram chooses σₜ² = β̃ₜ for t ≥ 2 and draws fresh Gaussian zₜ there; at t = 1 it sets z₁ = 0 and returns the mean without new noise. The training target ε and the fresh sampling noise zₜ play different roles. Boxes show the algorithm, not generated observations."
>
  <svg class="wide" viewBox="0 0 860 490" role="img" aria-labelledby="ddpm-sampling-wide-title ddpm-sampling-wide-desc">
    <title id="ddpm-sampling-wide-title">A reverse transition combines a predicted mean with fresh noise</title>
    <desc id="ddpm-sampling-wide-desc">Initialize xT from a standard Gaussian. The current xt and timestep t feed the noise predictor. Form the mean by subtracting beta_t times the prediction divided by square root of one minus alpha-bar_t, then dividing by square root of alpha_t. Add sigma_t times independent Gaussian z_t for t greater than one, using posterior variance beta-tilde_t. Set z1 to zero at the final step. Reuse the output as the next state and decrement the time until reaching x0.</desc>
    <defs><marker id="ddpm-sampling-wide-head" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="head" /></marker></defs>
    <rect x="30" y="25" width="220" height="56" rx="4" class="input" />
    <text x="140" y="59" text-anchor="middle">Initialize xT ∼ N(0, I)</text>
    <text x="555" y="56" text-anchor="middle" class="strong">Repeat for t = T, T−1, …, 1</text>
    <path d="M 110 81 V 132" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-sampling-wide-head)" />
    <g class="node"><rect x="30" y="140" width="160" height="90" rx="4" /><rect x="280" y="140" width="190" height="90" rx="4" /><rect x="560" y="140" width="270" height="90" rx="4" /></g>
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="110" y="176" class="strong">Current state xₜ</text><text x="110" y="203" class="muted">At noise level t</text><text x="375" y="171" class="strong">Noise predictor</text><text x="375" y="197">εθ(xₜ, t)</text><text x="375" y="217" class="muted">Conditioned on t</text><text x="695" y="170" class="strong">Form the mean μθ</text><text x="695" y="196">Subtract predicted noise</text><text x="695" y="217" class="muted">Then rescale by 1/√αₜ</text></g>
    <g class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-sampling-wide-head)"><path d="M 197 185 H 272" /><path d="M 477 185 H 552" /><path d="M 160 140 V 109 H 695 V 132" /></g>
    <text x="235" y="174" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Input</text><text x="515" y="174" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Predict</text><text x="430" y="101" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Keep xₜ in the mean formula</text>
    <text x="430" y="269" text-anchor="middle">μθ(xₜ, t) = [xₜ − βₜ εθ(xₜ, t) / √(1−ᾱₜ)] / √αₜ</text>
    <rect x="270" y="325" width="235" height="94" rx="4" class="input" />
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="387" y="352" class="strong">Fresh sampling noise zₜ</text><text x="387" y="379">t &gt; 1: draw N(0, I)</text><text x="387" y="402" class="muted">t = 1: use zero</text></g>
    <rect x="575" y="325" width="255" height="94" rx="4" class="node" />
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="702" y="353" class="strong">Next state xₜ₋₁</text><text x="702" y="384">μθ(xₜ, t) + σₜ zₜ</text><text x="702" y="406" class="muted">σₜ² = β̃ₜ for t ≥ 2</text></g>
    <g class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-sampling-wide-head)"><path d="M 695 277 V 317" /><path d="M 512 372 H 567" /></g>
    <text x="711" y="307" class="muted">Mean</text><text x="540" y="353" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">+ σₜ zₜ</text>
    <path d="M 830 386 H 846 V 451 H 110 V 237" class="loop" marker-end="url(#ddpm-sampling-wide-head)" />
    <text x="440" y="443" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Reuse the new state and decrement t</text>
    <text x="430" y="479" text-anchor="middle">At t = 1, return x₀ = μθ(x₁, 1) without adding fresh noise.</text>
  </svg>

  <svg class="narrow" viewBox="0 0 320 790" role="img" aria-labelledby="ddpm-sampling-narrow-title ddpm-sampling-narrow-desc">
    <title id="ddpm-sampling-narrow-title">A vertical reverse-sampling loop</title>
    <desc id="ddpm-sampling-narrow-desc">Begin at xT drawn from a standard normal distribution. For timesteps T down to one, predict epsilon from the current state and time, subtract its scaled contribution from xt and rescale to form the mean. Add fresh Gaussian noise scaled by the square root of the posterior variance at interior timesteps. At the last timestep add no noise. Repeat with the new state and finally return x0.</desc>
    <defs><marker id="ddpm-sampling-narrow-head" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="head" /></marker></defs>
    <text x="160" y="29" text-anchor="middle" class="strong">Start: xT ∼ N(0, I)</text>
    <text x="160" y="55" text-anchor="middle">Repeat t = T, …, 1</text>
    <rect x="42" y="90" width="236" height="64" rx="4" class="node" />
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="160" y="117" class="strong">Current state xₜ</text><text x="160" y="141" class="muted">At noise level t</text></g>
    <path d="M 160 161 V 189" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-sampling-narrow-head)" />
    <rect x="42" y="196" width="236" height="76" rx="4" class="node" />
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="160" y="223" class="strong">Predict εθ(xₜ, t)</text><text x="160" y="250" class="muted">Network receives xₜ and t</text></g>
    <path d="M 160 279 V 307" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-sampling-narrow-head)" />
    <rect x="42" y="314" width="236" height="137" rx="4" class="node" />
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="160" y="341" class="strong">Form μθ(xₜ, t)</text><text x="160" y="369">Start with xₜ, subtract</text><text x="160" y="398">βₜ εθ(xₜ, t) / √(1−ᾱₜ)</text><text x="160" y="426">then divide by √αₜ</text></g>
    <path d="M 160 458 V 486" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-sampling-narrow-head)" />
    <rect x="42" y="493" width="236" height="115" rx="4" class="input" />
    <g text-anchor="middle"><text x="160" y="520" class="strong">Add σₜ zₜ</text><text x="160" y="547">t &gt; 1: zₜ ∼ N(0, I)</text><text x="160" y="571" class="muted">Choose σₜ² = β̃ₜ for t ≥ 2</text><text x="160" y="596">t = 1: z₁ = 0</text></g>
    <path d="M 160 615 V 643" class="arrow" marker-end="url(#ddpm-sampling-narrow-head)" />
    <rect x="42" y="650" width="236" height="59" rx="4" class="node" />
    <text x="160" y="685" text-anchor="middle" class="strong">New state xₜ₋₁</text>
    <path d="M 278 679 H 307 V 121 H 285" class="loop" marker-end="url(#ddpm-sampling-narrow-head)" />
    <text x="160" y="742" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Loop: reuse state, decrement t.</text>
    <text x="160" y="773" text-anchor="middle">Last step: return the mean x₀.</text>
  </svg>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16px; }
  .strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .input { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .node { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .arrow, .head, .loop { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.7; stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .loop { stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .narrow { display: none; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) {
    .wide { display: none; }
    .narrow { display: block; max-width: 340px; margin-inline: auto; }
  }
</style>
